$NetBSD: README,v 1.0 2023/05/25 22:07:00 techav Exp $

This is a port of NetBSD to the Wrap030 homebrew 68030 computer by techav. It was forked from the cesfic port, with code brought in as needed from other m68k ports.

- MC68030 processor at 25MHz
- MC68882 coprocessor
- 16 Mbyte RAM
- 8 serial ports across two 16C554
- 1 MC6850 serial port (not supported) 
- IDE interface
- custom timer interrupt 

The port is very rudimentary. The kernel can be loaded by the ROM bootloader if converted by objcopy to a raw binary, renamed to BOOT.BIN, and copied to your directory of a FAT-formatted disk. No kernel boot arguments can be passed by the bootloader. Multiuser is not currently working. Console works on com0 for single-user.
